ing surface parking lots","x":287,"y":1155,"w":1805,"h":47},{"text":"with modern garages and add affordable homes above. Measure X inhibits bicycle and","x":284,"y":1214,"w":1678,"h":46},{"text":"pedestrian safety improvements. All told, Measure X would make it harder for families, seniors,","x":286,"y":1272,"w":1854,"h":46},{"text":"and people with disabilities to live and visit downtown.","x":285,"y":1331,"w":1067,"h":43},{"text":"Measure X is bad policy with no expiration date. Independent analysis finds it likely violates","x":286,"y":1423,"w":1774,"h":46},{"text":"state laws, risking millions in legal fees and years of delay. Taxpayers would foot the bill to","x":284,"y":1481,"w":1752,"h":45},{"text":"defend it, including endless appeals (no matter the merits). It could also put Menlo Park out of","x":284,"y":1539,"w":1838,"h":45},{"text":"compliance with state housing law, costing local control of development (and allowing builder's","x":283,"y":1597,"w":1858,"h":46},{"text":"remedy projects) city-wide.","x":284,"y":1656,"w":529,"h":43},{"text":"If approved, Measure X would:","x":284,"y":1745,"w":595,"h":44},{"text":"Block affordable homes downtown.","x":428,"y":1837,"w":689,"h":35},{"text":"Hinder Menlo Park's efforts to revitalize downtown like neighboring cities have.","x":428,"y":1895,"w":1544,"h":45},{"text":"Block much-needed downtown parking improvements.","x":428,"y":1953,"w":1066,"h":44},{"text":"Forever inhibit the city's ability to plan for downtown's future.","x":427,"y":2012,"w":1207,"h":44},{"text":"Delay even simple downtown projects like installing EV Chargers, by up to two years.","x":427,"y":2072,"w":1643,"h":45},{"text":"Complicate compliance with state law.","x":425,"y":2130,"w":748,"h":43},{"text":"Cost Menlo Park taxpayers millions in legal fees.","x":425,"y":2189,"w":932,"h":43},{"text":"Join trusted community leaders and organizations and Vote No on Measure X to support a","x":277,"y":2280,"w":1755,"h":44},{"text":"vibrant downtown and 